{"board":{"height":8,"width":8},"description":"Chess with four wolves. A wolf belongs to neither player: it stands on the board from the first move and, after every move either player makes, steps to the next square of its own five-square patrol, eating whatever it finds there. Two patrols circle each wing, and each is mirrored, so every player has a wolf pacing their own half of both. A wolf is not worth anything to take -- there is no bounty and no score to collect -- and only a knight can bring one down; a pawn, bishop, rook, queen or king that meets one has to go round. A square a wolf will step to next is a square no king may stand on.","name":"wolves","pieces":[{"captures":["P","N","B","R","Q","K"],"id":"P","moves":[{"kind":"slide","mode":"move","range":1,"vectors":[[0,1]]},{"condition":{"from_rank":1},"kind":"slide","min_range":2,"mode":"move","range":2,"vectors":[[0,1]]},{"kind":"leap","mode":"capture","symmetry":"lateral","vectors":[[1,1]]}],"name":"pawn","value":1},{"id":"N","moves":[{"kind":"leap","mode":"both","symmetry":"dihedral8","vectors":[[1,2]]}],"name":"knight","value":3},{"captures":["P","N","B","R","Q","K"],"id":"B","moves":[{"kind":"slide","mode":"both","symmetry":"rotate4","vectors":[[1,1]]}],"name":"bishop","value":3},{"captures":["P","N","B","R","Q","K"],"id":"R","moves":[{"kind":"slide","mode":"both","symmetry":"rotate4","vectors":[[1,0]]}],"name":"rook","value":5},{"captures":["P","N","B","R","Q","K"],"id":"Q","moves":[{"kind":"slide","mode":"both","symmetry":"rotate4","vectors":[[1,0],[1,1]]}],"name":"queen","value":9},{"captures":["P","N","B","R","Q","K"],"id":"K","moves":[{"kind":"leap","mode":"both","symmetry":"rotate4","vectors":[[1,0],[1,1]]}],"name":"king","royal":true,"value":0},{"id":"W","moves":[{"kind":"leap","mode":"both","symmetry":"dihedral8","vectors":[[1,0],[1,1]]}],"name":"wolf","value":3}],"provenance":{"added":"2026-09-07","history":"The calibration baseline for this project rather than its goal. Every measurement was no